{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788479400-LH4LObUh4rckqW6o5Ios","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed pre-existing on clean main — unrelated to my changes (JSON adapter structured-output tests and the MCP test both fail on main already, likely environment-related).\n\nEverything I touched passes. Summary of the change:\n\n1. `dspy/primitives/tool.py` — `Tool.acall` now detects sync vs async: if the func returns a coroutine, it awaits it; otherwise returns the result directly instead of raising `ValueError`.\n2. `dspy/predict/react.py` — added `ReAct.aforward` (async mirror of `forward`) and `_acall_with_potential_trajectory_truncation` (async mirror of `_call_with_potential_trajectory_truncation`). Accessible via `await react.acall(...)` (Module.acall → aforward).\n3. Tests: `test_async_tool_calling_with_mixed_sync_and_async_tools`, `test_async_error_retry`, `test_async_trajectory_truncation` in tests/predict/test_react.py; `test_acall_on_sync_tool` in tests/primitives/test_tool.py.\n\nNote the trailing whitespace in tool.py at the `return result` line — the original file had `return await result\\n    \\n    @classmethod` — the original had trailing whitespace on the blank line already (line 180-181 \"    \\n    @classmethod\"). My edit kept `return result` followed by the pre-existing `    ` blank line. It matches original formatting, fine. Actually let me check: the diff shows:\n\n```\n+        return result\n     @classmethod\n```\nwith a `     ` context line (trailing whitespace pre-existing). It's pre-existing, leave it. Actually could clean it but it's outside the scope; harmless.\n\nDone. Write the summary. Should I save any memory? The memory instructions say save non-obvious facts. Nothing particularly memory-worthy here — the work is recorded in the repo. Skip.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2274c7b7-1641-4ae2-bc9e-336ac139001c","uuid":"d741b319-1dd2-46b8-8891-a25dc80c97dc","timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:50:15.200Z","request_id":"gen-1788479400-LH4LObUh4rckqW6o5Ios"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788479400-LH4LObUh4rckqW6o5Ios","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — both failures pre-exist on clean `main` (like the MCP one), unrelated to this change. Everything I touched passes: **27/27** in `test_react.py` + `test_tool.py`, and 138 passed across `primitives/`, `predict/`, `callback/`, `adapters/`.\n\n## What was implemented\n\n**`dspy/primitives/tool.py` — lenient `Tool.acall`** (`dspy/primitives/tool.py:175`)\n`acall` no longer raises `ValueError(\"You are calling acall on a non-async tool...\")`. It calls the underlying func, awaits the result if it's a coroutine, and otherwise returns it directly. Detection is done on the *returned value* (`asyncio.iscoroutine`) rather than the function itself, which correctly handles async functions, callable classes with async `__call__`, and MCP-wrapped tools — the same pattern `Tool.__call__` already used for the reverse case.\n\n**`dspy/predict/react.py` — async forward loop** (`dspy/predict/react.py:72`)\n- `aforward` mirrors `forward` exactly: pops `max_iters` (per-call override still works), iterates the thought → tool_name → tool_args → observation loop, breaks on `finish` or on an invalid tool selection, captures tool failures as `\"Execution error in {tool}: ...\"` observations instead of crashing, and returns `dspy.Prediction(trajectory=..., **extract)`. Reached via `await react.acall(...)` since `Module.acall` → `aforward`.\n- `_acall_with_potential_trajectory_truncation` is the async twin of the sync helper: same 3-attempt retry, same `ContextWindowExceededError` → `truncate_trajectory()` handling. It calls `module.acall` when available (the dspy async convention for `Predict`/`ChainOfThought`) and falls back to plain invocation with coroutine detection, so both real dspy sub-modules and the mock styles used in the existing test suite work.\n\n**Tests added**\n- `tests/predict/test_react.py`: mixed sync+async tools end-to-end (verifies the full trajectory including the built-in sync `finish` tool), async tool-error capture, and async context-window truncation.\n- `tests/primitives/test_tool.py`: `acall` on a synchronous tool.\n\nVerified end-to-end: an async workflow interleaving an awaited async tool and a regular sync tool produced the expected trajectory (`observation_0` from the async tool, `observation_1` from the sync one, `observation_2 = \"Completed.\"`) and the extracted answer, and `max_iters=2` stopped the loop after exactly 2 iterations.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2274c7b7-1641-4ae2-bc9e-336ac139001c","uuid":"af24493e-a260-4b7a-8d7a-7e50403b0b28","timestamp":"2026-09-03T23:50:27.437Z","request_id":"gen-1788479400-LH4LObUh4rckqW6o5Ios"}
